# esp32-c5-wroom-1-n8r8-01 -- ESP32-C5-WROOM-1-N8R8, physical unit 01 (MAC 10:bd:a3:dd:ab:74).
#
# ONE OF TWO IDENTICAL C5 UNITS.  This manifest and esp32-c5-wroom-1-n8r8-00.manifest are the same
# ship-list; they are separate files only because the ENV is per-unit, and the env is per-unit so a
# flash and a result bind to ONE PHYSICAL BOARD.  Keep the two in sync -- if you change one, change
# the other, the same way the three esp32s3-n8r2*.manifest files are kept identical.
#
# HARDWARE IS IN HAND (arrived 2026-09-11).  The header this file inherited said
# "hardware ON ORDER" and "THIS SHIP-LIST HAS NEVER BEEN BOOTED", and went on to describe a C6
# devkit -- it had been cloned from esp32-c6-devkitc-1 and never re-based.  Two of its warnings were
# already false when read on 2026-09-11 and are corrected here rather than left to mislead:
#   * PIN MAP: it warned that `boards/pins/linux.scm` (the no-hardware STUB) was staged as Pins.scm.
#     It is not, and has not been since 2026-09-09 -- this manifest stages the real C5 pin map,
#     boards/pins/esp32-c5-wroom-1-n8r8.scm, read from Espressif's own esp32c5 Arduino variant.
#     That was B336.
#   * FILESYSTEM SIZE: it warned of partitions_4M.csv "inherited from flash_mb=4".  This target is
#     flash_mb=8 and takes the 8 MB partition table, so the WROVER's sectioned-test problem (suite
#     does not fit the FS at once) does not obviously apply.  Re-measure before assuming either way.
#
# MEMORY IS MEASURED, NOT INFERRED.  This unit was flashed on 2026-09-11 and printed its own
# report: `PSRAM free: 7917236 / 8388608`, `Flash size: 8192K` -- 8 MB of each, and the sibling
# unit reports the identical total.  That measurement is why this env is named N8R8: it was briefly
# named `-n8r4-` earlier the same day, from the module part number, before any board had been read.
# THE BOARD LINE IS `w3_board-esp32c5-n8r8`, a w3-local board type, because the platform ships no
# N8R8 definition and N8R4/N8R8 are different board types.  It was briefly pointed at the stock
# `esp32-c5-devkitc1-n8r4` on 2026-09-11 and reverted: that builds identical bytes -- PSRAM size is
# not expressible in a board JSON, ESP-IDF probes the chip at boot (B338) -- but it misnames the
# hardware wherever the board id is read or logged.  Do not re-make that swap.
# partitions_8M.csv is the right table and the flash is genuinely 8 MB.
#
# STILL TRUE AND STILL UNMEASURED: nothing in this list has been observed RUNNING on a C5.  The
# board arrived only days ago and P173 Phase 0 has not been executed.  Treat the module list as a
# starting point, not as a measurement.
#
# The module list mirrors the S3/WROVER core set because setup.scm loads most of these
# UNCONDITIONALLY (ESP32.scm, WiFi.scm, WS2812.scm, LightSensor.scm ...): omitting one does not
# make it optional, it makes the load fail.

# Core runtime
core/setup.scm
core/Compiler.scm
core/Lobs.scm
core/Behaviors.scm
core/Terminal.scm
file: boards/pins/esp32-c5-wroom-1-n8r8.scm -> Pins.scm
core/Timers.scm
core/ESP32.scm
core/CommonIO.scm
core/Sonar.scm
core/I2C.scm
core/Wire.scm
core/PCA9685.scm
core/PCF8574.scm
core/LCD1602.scm
core/Buzzer.scm
core/WiFi.scm
core/WS2812.scm
core/LightSensor.scm
core/array.scm

# R5RS/R7RS overrides
rxrs/rxrs.scm
rxrs/rxrs_cxr.scm
rxrs/rxrs_exceptions.scm
rxrs/rxrs_continuations.scm
rxrs/rxrs_promises.scm
rxrs/rxrs_quasiquote.scm
rxrs/rxrs_syntax.scm
rxrs/rxrs_library.scm
rxrs/rxrs_srfi.scm

# Serial file+command tunnel: resident LLIP receiver -- needed AT BOOT to accept pushed files,
# which is how the ll_tests suite reaches an embedded FS at all (w3_ai_scripts/llip_test_runner.py).
features/llip-serial.scm
features/csv.scm
features/dh_groups.scm
features/rsa.scm
features/Neopixel.scm

tools/test-framework.scm
tools/llip-server.scm

# Runtime defaults
runtime-defaults/Settings.scm
optional: runtime-defaults/Settings-local.scm -> Settings-local.scm
optional: runtime-defaults/net-test-ca.pem -> net-test-ca.pem
runtime-defaults/Settings-Lamb.scm

# Test suite -- the same lean embedded pattern as the S3 manifests: bench + the NCG fusion probe
# ride the FS image; the correctness tiers are pushed incrementally over LLIP.
file: tests/ll_tests/bench-runner.scm     -> ll_tests/bench-runner.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/benchmarks.scm       -> ll_tests/benchmarks.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/bignum-hw-probe.scm  -> ll_tests/bignum-hw-probe.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/bignum-hw-sweep.scm      -> ll_tests/bignum-hw-sweep.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/bignum-cost-probe.scm   -> ll_tests/bignum-cost-probe.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/bignum-hw-cliff.scm     -> ll_tests/bignum-hw-cliff.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/ncg-fusion-probe.scm -> ll_tests/ncg-fusion-probe.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/gc-pause-bench.scm   -> ll_tests/gc-pause-bench.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/pause_bench.scm      -> ll_tests/pause_bench.scm
